{
  "id": "y9-algorithms-l9",
  "label": "9CT.01 L9: Arrays - Farm Specific Spots",
  "steps": [
    {"id":"do-now","label":"Do Now: Nested Iteration Retrieval","type":"short-answer-validation","validatorId":"y9-algorithms-l9-do-now","validatorKey":"y9_algorithms_l9_do_now","content":"<h2 class=\"lesson-h2\">Do Now: Nested Iteration Retrieval</h2><p class=\"lesson-lead\">Quick recall from last lesson.</p><div class=\"lesson-do-now-responses\"><div class=\"lesson-do-now-response\"><label for=\"y9-algorithms-l9-do-now-a\">(a) FOR A &lt;- 1 TO 2 contains FOR B &lt;- 1 TO 3. How many total inner passes happen?</label><input id=\"y9-algorithms-l9-do-now-a\" class=\"lesson-exam-answer\" data-answer-id=\"y9-algorithms-l9-do-now-a\"></div><div class=\"lesson-do-now-response\"><label for=\"y9-algorithms-l9-do-now-b\">(b) A Grid Farm plants a rectangle. What shape can it NOT plant?</label><input id=\"y9-algorithms-l9-do-now-b\" class=\"lesson-exam-answer\" data-answer-id=\"y9-algorithms-l9-do-now-b\"></div></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"donow-btn\" id=\"y9-algorithms-l9-do-now-check\">Check answers</button><div id=\"y9-algorithms-l9-do-now-feedback\" class=\"pseudocode-feedback\" role=\"status\"></div>"},
    {"id":"title","label":"Arrays: Farm Specific Spots","content":"<div class=\"lesson-title-slide\"><p class=\"lesson-title-kicker\">Algorithms and Data</p><h2 class=\"lesson-h2\">Arrays: Farm Specific Spots</h2><p>Year 9, 9CT.01</p></div>"},
    {"id":"objectives","label":"Three Goals","content":"<h2 class=\"lesson-h2\">Three Goals</h2><div class=\"lesson-do-now-columns\"><div class=\"lesson-flow-task\"><h3>Store</h3><p>Keep a whole list of values under one name, using an <strong>array</strong>.</p></div><div class=\"lesson-flow-task\"><h3>Index</h3><p>Read or write one item in the list using its position, e.g. <code>Xs[2]</code>.</p></div><div class=\"lesson-flow-task\"><h3>Combine</h3><p>Use a FOR loop and an array together to visit any set of chosen spots.</p></div></div>"},
    {"id":"direct-instruction","label":"Array Syntax","content":"<h2 class=\"lesson-h2\">Array Syntax</h2><p class=\"lesson-lead\">A Strip Farm and a Grid Farm both farm a fixed, computed pattern. An <strong>array</strong> stores a whole list of values under one name, so you can farm any set of spots you choose instead.</p><div class=\"lesson-code\"><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">Xs[1] &lt;- 0</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">Xs[2] &lt;- 2</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">Zs[1] &lt;- 1</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">Zs[2] &lt;- 0</div></div><ul class=\"lesson-facts\"><li>The number in square brackets is the <strong>index</strong> - which item in the list.</li><li>Indexes count from 1, not 0.</li><li>Two arrays used together, with the same index, can store two matching values per spot - here, an X coordinate and a Z coordinate for the same point.</li><li>You read a value back the same way you wrote it: <code>Xs[1]</code> gives back 0.</li></ul>"},
    {"id":"worked-check","label":"Check: Read the Arrays","type":"short-answer-validation","validatorId":"y9-algorithms-l9-worked-check","validatorKey":"y9_algorithms_l9_worked_check","content":"<h2 class=\"lesson-h2\">Check: Read the Arrays</h2><div class=\"lesson-code\"><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">Xs[1] &lt;- 0</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">Xs[2] &lt;- 2</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">Zs[1] &lt;- 1</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">Zs[2] &lt;- 0</div></div><div class=\"lesson-do-now-responses\"><div class=\"lesson-do-now-response\"><label for=\"y9-algorithms-l9-worked-check-a\">(a) What value does Xs[2] give back?</label><input id=\"y9-algorithms-l9-worked-check-a\" class=\"lesson-exam-answer\" data-answer-id=\"y9-algorithms-l9-worked-check-a\"></div><div class=\"lesson-do-now-response\"><label for=\"y9-algorithms-l9-worked-check-b\">(b) Which spot do Xs[1] and Zs[1] together describe?</label><input id=\"y9-algorithms-l9-worked-check-b\" class=\"lesson-exam-answer\" data-answer-id=\"y9-algorithms-l9-worked-check-b\"></div></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"donow-btn\" id=\"y9-algorithms-l9-worked-check-button\">Check answers</button><div id=\"y9-algorithms-l9-worked-check-feedback\" class=\"pseudocode-feedback\" role=\"status\"></div>"},
    {"id":"farmer-tutorial","label":"Machine Tutorial: Array Farm","type":"app-link","buttonId":"y9-algorithms-l9-farmer-button","appId":"pseudocodefarmer","appQuery":"tutorial=array-farm","content":"<h2 class=\"lesson-h2\">Machine Tutorial: Array Farm</h2><p class=\"lesson-lead\">Open Pseudocode Farmer. It will take you straight into the Array Farm tutorial - follow every step in order.</p><div class=\"lesson-flow-task\"><h3>Complete when</h3><p>The tutorial panel says &quot;Tutorial complete&quot; and your machine keeps visiting the same two scattered spots, forever, on its own.</p></div><div class=\"lesson-app-link\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"donow-btn\" id=\"y9-algorithms-l9-farmer-button\">Open Pseudocode Farmer</button></div>"},
    {"id":"scaffold-fill-blank","label":"Fix the Index","type":"short-answer-validation","validatorId":"y9-algorithms-l9-fill-blank","validatorKey":"y9_algorithms_l9_fill_blank","content":"<h2 class=\"lesson-h2\">Fix the Index</h2><p class=\"lesson-lead\">This loop is meant to visit both stored spots, but it keeps visiting the same one twice.</p><div class=\"lesson-code\"><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">Xs[1] &lt;- 0</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">Xs[2] &lt;- 3</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">Zs[1] &lt;- 1</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">Zs[2] &lt;- 2</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">FOR i &lt;- 1 TO 2</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;CALL SetPosition(Xs[1], Zs[1])</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">NEXT i</div></div><label for=\"y9-algorithms-l9-fill-blank-a\">Rewrite the SetPosition line only, so each pass visits a different spot.</label><input id=\"y9-algorithms-l9-fill-blank-a\" class=\"lesson-exam-answer\" data-answer-id=\"y9-algorithms-l9-fill-blank-a\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"donow-btn\" id=\"y9-algorithms-l9-fill-blank-button\">Check answer</button><div id=\"y9-algorithms-l9-fill-blank-feedback\" class=\"pseudocode-feedback\" role=\"status\"></div>"},
    {"id":"independent-task","label":"Independent Task: Three Tomato Spots","type":"short-answer-validation","validatorId":"y9-algorithms-l9-independent","validatorKey":"y9_algorithms_l9_independent","content":"<h2 class=\"lesson-h2\">Independent Task: Three Tomato Spots</h2><p class=\"lesson-lead\">Write your own arrays and loop from scratch. No walkthrough this time.</p><div class=\"lesson-flow-task\"><h3>Requirement</h3><p>Using arrays named <code>Xs</code> and <code>Zs</code>, store these three spots: (1, 0), (0, 2), (2, 1). Then use a FOR loop with index <code>i</code> to buy and plant a Tomato at every one of them.</p></div><div class=\"pseudocode-check\"><label for=\"y9-algorithms-l9-independent-code\"><strong>Your arrays and loop</strong></label><textarea id=\"y9-algorithms-l9-independent-code\" class=\"lesson-exam-answer\" data-answer-id=\"y9-algorithms-l9-independent-code\" spellcheck=\"false\" rows=\"9\"></textarea><button type=\"button\" class=\"donow-btn\" id=\"y9-algorithms-l9-independent-check\">Check my answer</button><div id=\"y9-algorithms-l9-independent-feedback\" class=\"pseudocode-feedback\" role=\"status\"></div></div>"},
    {"id":"plenary","label":"Plenary: Arrays","type":"short-answer-validation","validatorId":"y9-algorithms-l9-plenary","validatorKey":"y9_algorithms_l9_plenary","content":"<h2 class=\"lesson-h2\">Plenary: Arrays</h2><div class=\"lesson-do-now-responses\"><div class=\"lesson-do-now-response\"><label for=\"y9-algorithms-l9-plenary-a\">(a) In Cambridge Pseudocode, what number does an array's first index start at?</label><input id=\"y9-algorithms-l9-plenary-a\" class=\"lesson-exam-answer\" data-answer-id=\"y9-algorithms-l9-plenary-a\"></div><div class=\"lesson-do-now-response\"><label for=\"y9-algorithms-l9-plenary-b\">(b) Why is an array plus a loop more flexible than a Grid Farm for choosing which tiles to farm?</label><input id=\"y9-algorithms-l9-plenary-b\" class=\"lesson-exam-answer\" data-answer-id=\"y9-algorithms-l9-plenary-b\"></div></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"donow-btn\" id=\"y9-algorithms-l9-plenary-button\">Check answers</button><div id=\"y9-algorithms-l9-plenary-feedback\" class=\"pseudocode-feedback\" role=\"status\"></div><p class=\"lesson-lead\">This completes the Sequence, Selection, Iteration, Nested Iteration and Arrays unit.</p>"}
  ],
  "validators": {
    "y9_algorithms_l9_do_now":[{"suffix":"a","pattern":{"__regex":true,"source":"^\\s*6\\s*$","flags":"i"},"feedback":"2 outer passes x 3 inner passes = 6."},{"suffix":"b","pattern":{"__regex":true,"source":"(?=.*(?:scatter|random|irregular|specific|any|arbitrary|not.*(?:line|rectangle|block))).*","flags":"i"},"feedback":"A Grid Farm can only plant a computed rectangle - it can't plant scattered, arbitrary spots."}],
    "y9_algorithms_l9_worked_check":[{"suffix":"a","pattern":{"__regex":true,"source":"^\\s*2\\s*$","flags":"i"},"feedback":"Xs[2] was set to 2."},{"suffix":"b","pattern":{"__regex":true,"source":"(?=.*0)(?=.*1).*","flags":"i"},"feedback":"Xs[1] is 0 and Zs[1] is 1 - together, the spot (0, 1)."}],
    "y9_algorithms_l9_fill_blank":[{"suffix":"a","pattern":{"__regex":true,"source":"call\\s*setposition\\s*\\(\\s*xs\\s*\\[\\s*i\\s*\\]\\s*,\\s*zs\\s*\\[\\s*i\\s*\\]\\s*\\)","flags":"i"},"feedback":"Use the loop variable i as the index, not a fixed 1, so each pass reads a different array slot: CALL SetPosition(Xs[i], Zs[i])."}],
    "y9_algorithms_l9_independent":[{"suffix":"code","pattern":{"__regex":true,"source":"(?=.*xs\\s*\\[\\s*1\\s*\\]\\s*(?:<-|←)\\s*1)(?=.*xs\\s*\\[\\s*2\\s*\\]\\s*(?:<-|←)\\s*0)(?=.*xs\\s*\\[\\s*3\\s*\\]\\s*(?:<-|←)\\s*2)(?=.*zs\\s*\\[\\s*1\\s*\\]\\s*(?:<-|←)\\s*0)(?=.*zs\\s*\\[\\s*2\\s*\\]\\s*(?:<-|←)\\s*2)(?=.*zs\\s*\\[\\s*3\\s*\\]\\s*(?:<-|←)\\s*1).*for\\s*i\\s*(?:<-|←)\\s*1\\s*to\\s*3[\\s\\S]*?call\\s*setposition\\s*\\(\\s*xs\\s*\\[\\s*i\\s*\\]\\s*,\\s*zs\\s*\\[\\s*i\\s*\\]\\s*\\)[\\s\\S]*?call\\s*buy\\s*\\(\\s*[\"']tomato[\"']\\s*\\)[\\s\\S]*?call\\s*plant\\s*\\(\\s*[\"']tomato[\"']\\s*\\)[\\s\\S]*?next\\s*i","flags":"is"},"feedback":"Check all three (X, Z) pairs are stored correctly, the loop runs 1 TO 3, and SetPosition/Buy/Plant all use the loop variable i and Tomato."}],
    "y9_algorithms_l9_plenary":[{"suffix":"a","pattern":{"__regex":true,"source":"^\\s*1\\s*$","flags":"i"},"feedback":"Cambridge Pseudocode arrays are indexed from 1, not 0."},{"suffix":"b","pattern":{"__regex":true,"source":"(?=.*(?:choose|any|specific|scatter|store|list|arbitrary)).*","flags":"i"},"feedback":"An array can store any set of coordinates you choose - the shape lives in the data, not a computed pattern in the code."}]
  }
